  "candidateNotes": [
    "v10 removed the direction factor from the alpha composition entirely (the last 0.4 on a negative residual; the recovery-conditioned 0.25 went earlier). Negative learning is now damped only by the K-consecutive confirmation count. This report is the single-factor evaluation the doc requires for that 2.5x change: compare acceptance.negativeOpportunitiesToFirstAcceptance and trueAbility across the v9 and v10 runs, and note that with zero labelled outcomes locally the question 'is faster negative learning better' stays not_evaluable — only the mechanical effect is measured.",
    "drop_efficiency is a weight-floor artifact, not an ability finding: dropping efficiency leaves pace + stability at 0.5 of the configured 0.875, below the 0.65 minimumAvailableWeight floor, so every attempted workout becomes trial and no CA is produced.",
    "acceptance denominators are the independent candidate opportunities taken before the gates decide. Every gate is implemented and applied: §6.7 evidence reliability, §6.2 stratum comparability, and the §6.9 K-consecutive negative confirmation. A high rate therefore means the gates rarely bind on this data, not that they are missing. A negative candidate counted as accepted is one whose update was actually applied — a residual deferred by the confirmation count is not acceptance.",
    "the per-stratum breakdown is reported in stratumCensus. A per-device correlation breakdown is not, because the feature contract carries no device dimension."
